#2404
A Corner in the Bandit Camp~
   You're at the northeastern corner of the camp, walled to your north by a
wooden-pole blockade, and to the east by a tent whose entrance is covered. A
small hawk eyes you from his perch atop the wall, disappointed at your animate
state. As a whole, the palette around here is pretty boring, not generally
venturing from the boring yellow of the sand and white of the tents.
  To some extent, you wish you had some paint to splash around here, in hopes
of livening things up a little. There is a small tent to your east, though
some flaps block your view of its contents.
~
