#2406
A Corner in the Bandit Camp~
   The scenery around here is pretty bland. White, weathered tents staked
into the sand on four sides, and of course, sand. The occasional black
scorpion scuttling across the sand isn't necessarily eye-catching, but it's a
bit of a change from the usual. A large supporting pole for the lookout's nest
provides a bit of shade here, but not enough to bother stopping to enjoy.
   Your north wall is the border of this outpost, and a tent prohibits exit to
the west. Off to your east is the entrance, and a field of training dummies,
while the south yields yet more sand, and a large tent with an equally large
opening.
~
