#2407
Sparring Grounds~
   The land here really isn't entirely different from any other area of the
camp, except that a small square area has been marked off by stakes and lines
drawn in the sand. A group of wooden swords rests against one of the tents,
some broken, others barely splintered, but all used. The sand in this area is
incredibly cratered, likely due to the footwork required of those who spar.
   Canteens rest at the west and east sides of the square, in convenient
positions for post-spar refreshment. Tent walls prevent travel to the east or
south, while the north and west both extend to further parts of the camp.
~
